# Ponytail (DealerHire)

Use Ponytail Full mode for normal implementation. Lite for architecture exploration. Ultra only for explicit deletion/simplification — never for auth, migrations, PII, compliance, accessibility, billing/spend, incident recovery, or destructive work.

## Hard floors (do not remove)

- Correctness, security, accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA), privacy, legal controls, operability
- PostgreSQL authority; acceptance envelope as sole application receipt
- Forced tenant/rooftop/purpose isolation
- Deterministic policy + employer authority; no direct AI ad actuation
- Candidate AI shadow-only until EmploymentAIUse gate
- Atomic approval → command → outbox; provider calls outside DB transactions
- No raw PII in immutable telemetry

## Prefer

- Server Components, native HTML controls, Web APIs, Cloudflare bindings, Postgres constraints
- One package, modules only when a vertical slice needs them
- Plain SQL migrations + thin typed query layer
- Extract helpers after repeated identical behavior

## Avoid

- Empty architecture folders, repository/service layers without a second implementation
- Queue-per-arrow, database-per-plane, full event-sourcing platforms
- Controller/arbiter/sensor microservices — use domain functions and tables

## After every pass (mandatory)

When an implementation/remediation pass finishes (code changed, verify claimed green, or a P0/P1 item marked done), **before stopping**:

1. Run a Ponytail Full audit of what just landed (not a full-repo archaeology dump).
2. Score hard floors Pass / Partial / Fail with paths.
3. Call out new smells or regressions from *this* pass.
4. Rank the next ≤5 Full-mode actions.

A project `stop` hook also auto-requests this audit when product/test/schema files are dirty. If the hook fires, produce the audit immediately; do not start unrelated work.
